{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Not one day etc.</b> Why are all these specifications said? For all of them add up to the full count of days that Israel were commanded [to rest]. 'One day' and 'two days' — that is 3; and 'five' — that is 8; and 'ten' — that is 18; and 'twenty days' — that is 38; and 'a month of days' — 29 days — that is 67 days. And according to this count, the Sabbaths and festivals in a year are as follows: there are 50 Sabbaths in a lunar year, which amounts to 54 days [of rest]; and 4 from Passover, and 2 days from Shavuot, and 2 days from Rosh HaShanah, and 1 of Yom HaKippurim — that is 59; and 4 from Sukkot — that is 63; and 4 Sabbaths from the intercalary month — that is 67. This is what it says: the Merciful One included all those days — (that he eat the days) that they shall eat the flesh on all those days, no blemish shall befall them. And to me it appears one should explain: 'not one day' — there shall not be for you eating on Yom HaKippurim; and 'not two days' — the two days of Shavuot, which are a day of rejoicing before Him; or alternatively, the two days of Rosh HaShanah, which are days of remembrance before Him; and 'not five days' — the five days between Yom HaKippurim and Sukkot, and the day of Sukkot is included, which are days of rejoicing for Israel because their sins were forgiven; and 'not ten' — the ten days of repentance; and 'not twenty days' — that is 21 days on which they shall have no eating, the 21 days on which Israel complete the Hallel in the diaspora, which are days of rejoicing for Israel. And therefore it writes יום and does not write ימים, as with the others."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The parenthesis '(שיאכל הימים)' appears to be a variant or corrupt insertion; translated hyper-literally as it stands. The final arithmetic yields 21 from 1+2+5+10+3 (the three pilgim festivals being included in prior counts); the compiler's own counting is preserved as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:14.051689365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}